{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/345940-prometheans-running-an-orphanage","id":345940,"title":"Prometheans running an orphanage.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-20T11:17:30-08:00","id":345940,"title":"Prometheans running an orphanage.","content":"Just to clarify this would be taking place in the modern United States, so actually it would be a foster home.<br /> <br /> But yeah. I told my players that children have less of a reaction to the Pyros than adults do ala the little girl in Frankenstein and they immediately decided that they wanted to run an orphanage for un-adoptable children in our game. I said that was fine but what should I know going into this? I have never run a Promethean game before and I could use some help figuring out what unique challenges and advantages they would have running a stationary home for fostered youths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:55:44-08:00","id":345991,"title":"","content":"One thing that immediately comes to mind is that with reduced reaction to Promethean Disquiet comes reduced reaction to Pandoran Disquiet.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking monsters in the walls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T12:17:26-08:00","id":346022,"title":"","content":"I had been thinking that their house would be in constant disrepair due to the effects of stationary and building pyros. Neither character has high craft for repairs so I was considering a pandoran &quot;house pet&quot; like Lurch in the Adams family who managed repairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:38:06-08:00","id":346070,"title":"","content":"While the kids might find it easier to resist, social services does not have such benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:47:53-08:00","id":346075,"title":"","content":"yeah Im trying to justify that part. From what little I know about foster homes social workers still need to come around every so often to check on things. My thought is that either they've found some way around that (corrupt official, special status as a permanent home etc) or that they pay a normal human to be their representative when the social worker comes, someone who can stand the effects of pyros long enough to collect a large stack of cash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T15:46:19-08:00","id":347039,"title":"","content":"It doesn't need to be someone who can stand the Pyros necessarily. Someone shady enough might cover for enough pay, whatever they suspect about the goings-on there. There's some potential mileage in such a character being able to sway social services while the much kinder Prometheans cannot (assuming they <i>are</i> kind about it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T23:05:51-08:00","id":347170,"title":"","content":"The characters in general intend to be kind. They see human adults as dangerous and scary, but this is also how many human children see human adults. There is a kinship there and a desire to protect which I'm really looking forward to playing in the Promethean narrative.<br /> <br /> I like this idea of a shady character who is the &quot;face&quot; of the foster home but is themselves a very untrustworthy sort. Maybe I could do a story where this person starts demanding more money or threatens one of the children and the players have to decide between protecting their own secrecy or their charges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T23:36:29-08:00","id":347172,"title":"","content":"How complicated do you want the themes to be? From experience I have had working with youth in the child welfare system I can think of some:<br /> <br /> (1) Being an outsider. Youth in the child welfare system have generally suffered through horrific abuse and, in addition to that, quite often have Fetal Alcohol Spectrum Disorder and possibly some form of mental illness. As such, many of these youth are developmentally delayed and a person with the body of a sixteen year old but the mind of someone between, as an example, four to ten years old does not relate well and is not accepted by their peers in a regular school setting. As well, although these youth are not physically capable of performing some actions due to the brain damage caused by FASD as they look physically capable people put expectations on them that are quite often as viable as expecting someone in a wheelchair to just get up and walk. Due to this a lot of these youth just don't fit in with their peers; something a Promethean could relate to.<br /> <br /> (2) Impulse control. Quite often youth in the child welfare system have problems with impulse control due to the brain damage they have suffered from FASD. Many can be violent and lash out; the common causes for this are brain damage, the abuse the youth suffered, or a combination of the two. If its due to brain damage its a physical cause that the youth has to learn to work with. As a Promethean who is in Torment can do things they normally wouldn't do as a supernatural aspect of their condition overrules their normal impulses they could find similarities there.<br /> <br /> (3) What makes a person who they are? In my opinion, and not based on any scientific studies but solely my experiences so take it as you will, certain personality traits of a person come through despite what has happened to them. There was a youth I worked with who had suffered through abuse that would sound more like it was in a gruesome movie than in real life and the youth was one of the nicest youth I worked with. Despite the huge developmental delays, terrible abuse suffered as a very young child, and mental illnesses the youth was a very caring person. Some other youth who had not suffered a fraction of what this youth had gone through or had had a small part of the problems this youth had had a predatory attitude towards everyone around them. Some youth, although they had huge problems fitting into society, were great with others and some were so dangerous to their peers that they had to be in one on one settings. With the youth that were predatory to those around them some stayed like that and some became better people. What makes people who they are? As Prometheans are attempting to gain humanity and find out who they are that is a question they might find themselves asking.<br /> <br /> (4) The inhumanity of humans and either rising above it or perpetuating it. Basically if you think of a form of abuse without a supernatural component then it has probably happened to someone already. A lot of the backgrounds of the youth I dealt with sounded more like they came from a movie or TV show but they did happen in the real world; not a fictional World of Darkness. While some of the youth will attempt to do to others what was done to them others will try to be better. If you would like to you could treat the idea of systemic neglect as although the people who are within the system generally want the best treatment for the youth the goal of the people funding the system is generally to save money. These goals are quite often not compatible. In general, Prometheans are attempting to emulate humanity so what happens when they see evidence of people who, while human, have done incredibly horrible things to other people? How about when they see people who could help but choose not to as it is easier not to see? How do Prometheans react to this and how does it affect their view of humanity? Do the Prometheans view humanity as noble or as something that can be noble or can also be its opposite?<br /> <br /> If you do want to deal with any of these themes then I would use the same caveat that I think I read in Asylum; be mindful of your group's comfort level and that situations based on real life can be very disturbing and can require a lot of sensitivity. Even if you move away from the themes of abuse then thinking that that child who, as an example, is physically sixteen, has the mental level, ability, and interests of a ten year old due to the brain damage the child suffered as a fetus in a womb and due to this is teased, tormented, and ostracized becomes a lot more disturbing when you realize this is something that happens every day.<br /> <br /> I don't know how much of that will be helpful to you (honestly, I think some of it would be very difficult to communicate effectively in a story) and I don't know what your group would consider fun but hopefully at least some of it proves to be useful to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T16:12:52-08:00","id":348611,"title":"","content":"Vedic: I'm going to print this post out and carry it around with me when I'm planning stories in this setting. I had an inkling on some of this but actually hearing from someone who has worked in this field is totally different. I doubt my group would be able handle getting too deep into some of these ideas but these themes are incredibly solid I would read this story if you wrote it as a book with no pulled punches. Thank you, thank you, <i>thank you</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T16:47:05-08:00","id":348626,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I'm glad it was useful for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T06:53:06-08:00","id":349030,"title":"","content":"Wow- after reading through that, it strikes me exactly how perfect those themes are for a Promethean game, and is making me kick myself for not noticing it before. It could even work as a good framework for a Pilgrimage. Perhaps in aiding the children of the foster home, the Prometheans come to an understanding of themselves, and that allows them to complete the Magnum Opus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}